+# Multimodal / Generative / Agentic / Physical AI Starter Components
+
+This patch adds starter components and stubs to help move Aegis from a promising foundation toward production-grade multimodal, generative, agentic and physical AI.
+
+What is included
+- Embedding service (FAISS-backed lightweight) and a LangChain retriever integration (langchain_runtime/rag_retriever.py).
+- Preprocessing microservices:
+  - Image frame extractor (preprocessing/image_frame_extractor.py)
+  - Audio featurizer stub (preprocessing/audio_featurizer.py)
+- Hallucination verifier service (verifier/hallucination_verifier.py) — heuristic evidence overlap check.
+- Agent sandbox (agent/sandbox_service.py) with OPA check and MCP logging of actions (opa/policies/agent_actions.rego).
+- ROS2 lifecycle manager stub (ros2/lifecycle_manager.py) to publish lifecycle events to Aegis ingest.
+- Timescale ingest helper (timeseries/ingest_timescale.py) to store telemetry.
+- HIL runner orchestrator (hil/hil_runner.py) that runs test scripts, stores output and attaches to MCP.
+
+Quickstart notes
+- Start the embedding service and point EMB_SRV to it from LangChain runtime.
+- Deploy verifier, sandbox and OPA, and configure OPA URL in agent sandbox (OPA bundle examples exist in repo).
+- For multimodal demo: extract frames -> index embeddings -> run retrieval -> call LangChain runtime with retrieved docs -> run verifier -> decide approval via A2A if needed.
+- For HIL: use hil/hil_runner.py to run scenario and inspect MCP records for attached artifacts.
+
+Security / Production considerations
+- Replace FAISS local index with managed vector DB (Milvus/Weaviate) for scale & HA.
+- Replace heuristic verifier with model-based fact-checking and robust retrieval.
+- Run action sandbox workers in isolated, instrumented environments and enforce OPA policies plus RBAC.
+- For physical AI, build PREEMPT_RT nodes, implement time sync (PTP), and run HIL extensively before any field deployment.
+
